    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25573" root="ضجع" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَضْجَعُ الثَّنَايَا</span></b>  (tropical:)  <i>Having the central incisors inclining;</i> (O, K, TA;) applied to a man: (O:)
pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضُجْعٌ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَضْجَعُ</span> signifies also
<i>Contrarious to his wife.</i> (O, K. [See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَجُوعٌ</span>.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  For a meaning of its fem., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَجْعَآءُ</span>,
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَاجِعٌ</span>, last sentence but one.

